// Fuzzer stub for triton::utils::fromUintToBuffer overloads (uint80/uint128/uint256/uint512)
// Contract: buffer is non-null and has at least 10/16/32/64 writable bytes respectively.
// Strategy:
//  - Build uint80/128/256 values from fuzzed byte buffers via cast<T>(const uint8_t*).
//  - Serialize them back with fromUintToBuffer() and validate round-trip equality using cast<T>(buffer).
//  - For uint512, avoid FUZZ_PARAM on class types; build value from smaller primitives, serialize, and assert non-zero byte presence iff value!=0.
{
